    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d155-a1">

                <pb facs="0288" n="176" xml:id="pg176"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Wai-wu Pu to the Chinese Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-06-24"><hi rendition="#italic">June 24,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your telegraphic report on the remission of the indemnity having been laid before
                    the Emperor, you are commanded to convey to the President of the United States
                    His Majesty’s warm thanks for this noble exhibition of his friendship toward
                    China, which is deeply and gratefully appreciated, by having alone taken the
                    lead in a matter of international justice.</p>
            </div>
